description:
Design a four-input NAND gate using two 2-input NAND gates followed by a combination of outputs to achieve the final output. The module takes two 2-bit inputs, A and B, and computes the intermediate NAND outputs before producing a single output, nand_out, that represents the NAND logic across the four input bits. The final output will be LOW only when all inputs are HIGH, reflecting the true characteristics of a four-input NAND gate.
module top_module(
  input [1:0] A,
  input [1:0] B,
  output nand_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [1:0] A,
  input [1:0] B,
  output nand_out
);wire [1:0] nand1_out;
wire nand2_out;

// Corrected the instantiation of the nand gate connecting to inputs A and B,
// using the proper inputs for a 2-input NAND gate.
nand nand1 (nand1_out[0], A[0], B[0]);
nand nand1_1 (nand1_out[1], A[1], B[1]);

// Combine the outputs of nand1 with a 2-input NAND gate
nand nand2 (nand2_out, nand1_out[0], nand1_out[1]);

// Final NAND operation for output
nand nand3 (nand_out, nand2_out, nand2_out);

endmodule

