description:
Design a 5-bit wide register selector that determines the output WriteReg based on the values of inputs rt, rd, and a 2-bit control signal RegDst. The module has three functional options: if RegDst is 00, it outputs a fixed value of 31; if RegDst is 01, it outputs the value of rt; and if RegDst is 10, it outputs the value of rd. If RegDst is any other value, the output retains its previous state.
module top_module(
    rt, rd, RegDst, WriteReg
);

code:
module top_module(
    rt, rd, RegDst, WriteReg
);input [4:0] rt;
    input [4:0] rd;
    input [1:0] RegDst;
    output reg[4:0] WriteReg;

    always @(rt or rd or RegDst)begin
        case(RegDst)
                   2'b00: WriteReg = 5'b11111;   
                   2'b01: WriteReg = rt;         
                   2'b10: WriteReg = rd;         
                   default: WriteReg = WriteReg;
        endcase       
    end
endmodule

